body:
I don't know what happened with **getPrimaryService**. The log from chrome stops after **getPrimaryService**. I check the log from the platform and chrome at the same time. However, the notify from device is received successfully based on the log from the platform. (see file btmon.btsnoop) 

I can't retrieve the received data if i don't get the service...
And I've read the many relevant issues but I still cannot solve it.

**log from the platform:**
[btmon.btsnoop.zip](https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/files/605804/btmon.btsnoop.zip)

**part of the code:**
`
	navigator.bluetooth.requestDevice({filters: [{services: ['battery_service']}]})
	.then(device => {
		this.device = device;
		console.log('> Found ' + this.device.name);
		console.log('Connecting to GATT Server...');
		//console.log(device.gatt.connect());
		return device.gatt.connect();
	})
		.then(server => {
		console.log('Getting server...'+server.connected);
		this.server = server;
		
		console.log('server device: '+this.server.device);
		//console.log('Getting service...'+service.uuid);
		//wait(3000);
		console.log('server device: '+this.server.device);
		return Promise.all([
			wait(3000),
			console.log('after 3 second '),		
			server.getPrimaryService(0x180f)
			.then(service => {
				console.log('service get');
				console.log(service.uuid);
			  return this._cacheCharacteristic(service, 'battery_level');
			}),
			console.log('after getPrimaryService '),
		])
			.then(values => { console.log('value' + values); });
	})
`
I'm using ubuntu 16.04 LTS with google-chrome-unstable 56.0.2922.1 dev (64-bit)
